  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nIn the browser (wasm) build the File commands did nothing: every picker went through `file_dialog.rs`, whose wasm half answers \"cancelled\" and only logs why. Now:\r\n\r\n- **Save, Save As and Post download.** The app layer gains `project::save_text` and `posting::post_setup_unwritten` - the same collect, the same gate and engine run, bytes held in memory. The desktop's `save` / `post_setup` now call them and write the result, so the two cannot drift. The UI hands the bytes to the browser (`crates/ui/src/browser_files.rs`: `Blob` + `URL.createObjectURL` + a hidden `a[download]` click, through `eframe::web_sys`; no new dependency). Save As asks for the name with `window.prompt`. A downloaded document is marked clean; the unsaved prompt's Save downloads too. A refused post offers nothing and opens the refusal window, as on the desktop.\r\n- **Everything else is refused by name and visibly disabled.** `browser_files::refusal` is the one table: opening anything (model, project, fixture, machine, post, theme, tool library, tool body) needs the browser file picker (#31, PR #1314); recent files, the fixture library folder and the per-operation folder post cannot exist in a page; setup sheet / tool list / stock STL / tool library exports are not downloads yet (#1437). `State::run` refuses those on the status line before anything else; ribbon cells (Model, Project, Post when per-op) are darkened with the reason as their tip; page buttons are greyed with the reason as their hover text. Context-menu rows and the theme dropdown's Browse row refuse on the status line only.\r\n- `State::browser_build` (set from `cfg!(target_arch = \"wasm32\")`) carries the law, so the native tests drive it.\r\n\r\nInventory of every dialog call site and what the browser did: issue comment on #1431. Decisions: `docs/decisions/1431-wasm-file-commands.md`.\r\n\r\n**Not stacked on PR #1314** (a contributor's fork branch). The open paths stay owed to it; when it lands, its commands come off `browser_files::refusal`. Hence `Refs #1431`, not `Fixes`.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/unwritten_post.rs`: `the_unwritten_post_is_the_written_program_byte_for_byte`, `the_unwritten_post_refuses_where_the_written_one_does`, `save_text_is_the_saved_project_file` - 3 passed.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/browser_files.rs` unit tests: `every_picker_and_folder_command_is_refused_by_name_in_the_browser`, `a_download_name_is_one_clean_segment_with_its_extension`.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/browser_files.rs` (structural): `the_ribbon_darkens_open_in_the_browser_and_says_why`, `open_in_the_browser_is_refused_by_name_not_ignored`, `save_downloads_the_project_text_and_marks_the_document_clean`, `post_downloads_the_gated_program_and_a_refusal_offers_nothing`, `a_per_op_post_is_refused_in_the_browser_and_the_cell_says_why`, `a_file_button_is_greyed_with_its_reason_in_the_browser` - 8 passed with the unit tests.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 673 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored. `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test coolant` and the project file suites touched by `save_text`: 7 and 73 passed.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The real browser: no wasm build was loaded in a browser; the download (`Blob` / anchor click), `window.prompt` and the greyed controls are unseen on the page. **Screenshots are owed for the maintainer** (the File ribbon and the greyed page buttons look different on wasm) before `/merge-ready` offers this PR.\r\n- `cargo check -p camcraft-ui --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` did not get past `flecs_ecs_sys` (its C build finds no `assert.h` without the wasm sysroot `web/build-app-wasm.sh` sets up), so the `#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]` half of `browser_files.rs` (the `web_sys` Blob / anchor / prompt calls) is not compiled here. The wasm build at the next cut (or `web/build-app-wasm.sh`) is its first compile.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Browser build: Save and Save As download the project, Post downloads the NC program, and file commands the browser cannot run yet are greyed with the reason instead of doing nothing (#1431)\r\n\r\nEffort: high (not escalated)\r\n\r\nRefs #1431\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
